def client_launch(port):
    """Step 13's second instance. A CLIENT that still opens a SERVER socket.

    That is not a typo and it is the last piece of the 2026-09-06 collision.
    The engine opens its server socket on `hostport` in EVERY instance, listen
    client included, so a second client launched with no -port sits on 27015 --
    and is then the game a PEER lane's second client connects to. Measured on
    the first green run of this fix: this gate's own server was on 27811 and
    something in the sampler still held 27015 for the length of the run. It was
    this instance.

    No -condebug: ONLY ONE instance may have it or both write
    bin/<config>/mods/test/console.log and neither log is then about one game.
    """
    return ["-debugapi", "-debugapisocket", "-nomessagebox", "-nocrashdialog",
            "-insecure", "-novid", "-windowed", "-w", "640", "-h", "480",
            "-port", str(port)] + strict_port_flags() + no_hltv_flags() + \
